This part alone would make the helm more powerful.

> Next, it (still) autocurses. 
> Lastly, when it is removed from your head, it automatically 
> disintegrates (also when, for example, stolen by a nymph).

That last part is the one that makes the helm quite uninteresting
(then you could as well remove the auto-cursing you propose above
because it becomes meaningless in the light on it's one-time
application).

> This would make it less reliable to change your alignment as expected 
> now, and limit its use to just once. Finally, the fact that it does not 
> disintegrate when you put it on, makes sure that you cannot put on 
> another hat until you've solved your problem.

For Astral the helm would become quite uninteresting (and risky
to use if you consider the loss of intrinsic protection[*]).

